---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Permit Expediting & Code Consulting for Owners, Architects & GCs" description="Burnham Nationwide supports owners, architects, engineers, contractors and municipalities with permit expediting, code consulting, licensing and approvals nationwide." nav="who-we-help">
  <div class="page-band">
    <div class="wrap">
      <ol class="crumbs"><li><a href="/">Home</a></li><li>Who we help</li></ol>
      <nav aria-label="On this page"><a href="#owners">Owners</a><a href="#architects-engineers">Architects &amp; engineers</a><a href="#contractors">Contractors</a><a href="#municipalities">Municipalities</a></nav>
    </div>
  </div>

  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="wrap grid grid--2 grid--center">
      <div class="stack">
        <h1 class="h-display">Service, every <span class="hl-block">step of the way.</span></h1>
        <p class="lede">From new construction to code compliance and building violations, Burnham Nationwide works with everyone who has a stake in getting a project approved.</p>
        <div class="row">
          <a class="btn btn--primary" href="/contact/">Start a project</a>
          <a class="btn btn--outline" href="/portfolio/">See our work</a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="link-rows" style="--min: 220px;">
        <a href="#owners"><span class="link-rows__title">Owners</span><span class="body">Developers, building managers, owners and agents.</span></a>
        <a href="#architects-engineers"><span class="link-rows__title">Architects &amp; engineers</span><span class="body">Permit applications and code consulting handled for you.</span></a>
        <a href="#contractors"><span class="link-rows__title">Contractors</span><span class="body">Permits, licensing and public way, sequenced to the schedule.</span></a>
        <a href="#municipalities"><span class="link-rows__title">Municipalities</span><span class="body">Third-party plan review for complex projects.</span></a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--dark section--tight">
    <div class="wrap grid grid--2 grid--center">
      <div class="stack stack--sm">
        <div class="eyebrow">Every stakeholder</div>
        <p class="h-section" style="font-size: clamp(24px, 2.6vw, 34px); line-height: 1.25;">We keep owners, municipalities, and design and construction teams working from the same information.</p>
      </div>
      <p class="body">Our expediters review every submittal package for completeness and accuracy, monitor plan review, and send the project team regular updates and any corrective measures required. Plans and supporting documents are archived in secure cloud storage that works with municipal online portals, available around the clock.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" id="owners">
    <div class="wrap grid grid--2 grid--center">
      <div class="stack">
        <span class="chip">Owners</span>
        <h2 class="h-section">Peace of mind for every permit, code and license.</h2>
        <p class="body">Getting a project running takes a thorough understanding of each jurisdiction’s requirements. With offices nationwide, our teams know local permitting regulations and use that knowledge to reduce project cycle time and cost.</p>
        <p class="body">We support the entire life cycle of a project and work with every vested party:</p>
        <ul class="tags"><li class="tag">Developers</li><li class="tag">Building managers</li><li class="tag">Owners &amp; agents</li></ul>
        <p class="body">That includes owners and asset managers delivering high-stakes assets such as data centers, where approval delays directly affect revenue and service commitments. Our in-house <a class="link" href="/what-we-do/code-consulting/">code consultants</a> can review projects and advise on code provisions.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="media media--tall"><img src="/assets/img/services/owners.jpg" alt="An owner in a suit walking a manufacturing floor with a worker in a safety vest" width="1500" height="1001" loading="lazy"></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--muted" id="architects-engineers">
    <div class="wrap grid grid--2 grid--center">
      <div class="media media--tall"><img src="/assets/img/services/due-diligence.jpg" alt="Architects marking up drawings with a compass and pens" width="1500" height="1000" loading="lazy"></div>
      <div class="stack">
        <span class="chip">Architects &amp; engineers</span>
        <h2 class="h-section">You design. We handle the approvals.</h2>
        <p class="body">Project architects and engineers have a lot on their plates. Burnham manages the administrative work of preparing permit applications, provides extensive code consulting and advises on special projects when needed.</p>
        <p class="body">Long-standing relationships with municipal departments, utilities and other stakeholders make securing approvals more efficient. We frequently partner with design firms on technically intensive work, including data centers that require careful coordination of structural, MEP and life safety codes across jurisdictions.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" id="contractors">
    <div class="wrap grid grid--2 grid--center">
      <div class="stack">
        <span class="chip">Contractors</span>
        <h2 class="h-section">Keep crews working while plans are finalized.</h2>
        <p class="body">With more than 30 years of experience, we guide construction teams through permitting, licensing and public way projects to avoid delays and keep work moving. We work with:</p>
        <ul class="tags"><li class="tag">Project managers</li><li class="tag">Construction managers</li><li class="tag">Subcontractors</li></ul>
        <div class="callout">
          <div class="callout__title">Phased permitting</div>
          <div class="callout__body">Burnham pioneered phased permitting, so construction runs continuously instead of waiting for every plan to be complete.</div>
        </div>
        <p class="body">For general contractors and construction managers building or retrofitting data centers, we sequence permits and inspections so critical-path interior work, including MEP rooms, generators, UPS and cooling infrastructure, stays on schedule.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="media media--tall"><img src="/assets/img/services/contractors.jpg" alt="Three contractors in hard hats reviewing drawings beside a surveying instrument" width="1500" height="791" loading="lazy"></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--muted" id="municipalities">
    <div class="wrap grid grid--2 grid--center">
      <div class="media media--tall"><img src="/assets/img/services/municipalities.jpg" alt="A domed brick city hall with American flags" width="1500" height="1000" loading="lazy"></div>
      <div class="stack">
        <span class="chip">Municipalities</span>
        <h2 class="h-section">Third-party plan review for complex projects.</h2>
        <p class="body">Many cities now use outside plan review firms to evaluate their most complex permit applications. As recognized plan review experts, Burnham serves as a municipal third-party reviewer for a wide variety of large-scale projects. Partnering with Burnham helps municipalities:</p>
        <ul class="list">
          <li>Improve communication with permit applicants</li>
          <li>Standardize the permit application process</li>
          <li>Use outside resources to improve permitting performance</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="body">Efficient permitting depends on active collaboration between municipal officials, applicants, consultants and other stakeholders. That collaboration is our everyday work.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap cta-block">
      <div class="stack stack--sm">
        <h2>Tell us where you sit on the project.</h2>
        <p>Owner, designer, builder or building department, a project manager will show you how Burnham fits in.</p>
      </div>
      <a class="btn btn--primary" href="/contact/">Contact us today</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
